            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0830" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/160: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sydney</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sydney</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-21T10:00:00+10:00">May 21, 1936—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 20—11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Prime Minister has now indicated that he will present to Parliament Friday
                    afternoon or evening an amending tariff schedule designed to correct to some
                    extent the adverse balance of trade with America. The new duties will become
                    effective as soon as tabled but must be validated by Parliament within 6 months
                    in order not to lapse. Although the new schedule is a closely guarded secret the
                    best opinion available is that the “general tariff” rather will be substantially
                    increased on a selected list of items of which we are the predominant supplier,
                    with emphasis on luxury and semi-luxury products.</p>
                <p>Throughout the past 6 weeks editorial opinion has continued to caution against
                    action directed exclusively at our trade; the Government’s <pb facs="0831"
                        n="751" xml:id="pg751"/> supporters in Parliament on the other hand have
                    been almost unanimous in pressing Lyons to take drastic action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moffat</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
